        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='0'] .slide-body",
          "source": "Answers are only the beliefs which One has proven to themselves through testing\n                  and direct observation (e.g., the Scientific Method) to a degree which they can\n                  personally validate the phenomenon exists,",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='0'] .slide-body em",
          "source": "for them",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='1'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Very Few Accepted Answers",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='1'] .slide-body",
          "source": "Accepted Answers are Answers which can be proven by repeated experimentation\n                  and largely acceptable in any open-minded, but serious, peer-reviewed journal.",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='2'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Open-Mindedness Is Essential",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='2'] .slide-body",
          "source": "Acknowledge that Science is still in its infancy and may or may not be the\n                  end-all-be-all. Beliefs should not be dismissed out of hand unless experimentation\n                  can be devised to prove otherwise in all instances. Even then, a benefit of the\n                  doubt that any given phenomenon may be real for any number of Observers should\n                  be afforded to them.",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='3'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Maintain Your Own Mythology",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='3'] .slide-body",
          "source": "While realizing we individually know Vanishingly Little, we must take care to\n                  consciously and continually maintain our own personal mythology system.",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='3'] .slide-body strong",
          "source": "A healthy mind is one which acknowledges it knows very little, considers\n                  many possibilities without prematurely collapsing uncertainty, and “continually\n                  follows the Truth, wherever it leads” [Thomas Jefferson].",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='3'] .slide-body",
          "source": "Do not believe anything without careful thought, feeling, and wherever possible,\n                  at least a little experimentation.",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='4'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Sustainability Is Crucial",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='4'] .slide-body",
          "source": "It is abundantly clear that the human footprint on this planet is causing\n                  irreparable harm to every ecosystem, potentially fatally. Every effort should be\n                  made to reduce our individual and collective footprints, including the disavowing\n                  of certain Beliefs that are easily perceived as promoting unsustainability\n                  (e.g., “The Earth was given to Man to do as He wilt.”).",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='5'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Reincarnation Is Preferred",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='5'] .slide-body",
          "source": "Few beliefs promote long-term Sustainability more: Belief in Reincarnation has\n                  been shown to dramatically increase the timeline horizons of its believers, from\n                  the common 5–10 years to over 500 to 1,000 years, as belief would necessitate\n                  living with one’s actions for thousands of years into the future. It also neatly\n                  ties up several hard-to-answer human dilemmas, such as the unfairness of being\n                  born severely handicapped.",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='6'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Many Paths That Are Not Equal",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='6'] .slide-body",
          "source": "There are many paths to a productive, fulfilling, sustainable life. UNICON seeks\n                  to discover the more efficient ones while advocating against the more destructive\n                  paths.",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='7'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Theistic Belief Is Non-Essential",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='7'] .slide-body",
          "source": "Personal belief in deity is understood and accepted, but it is not advocated at\n                  this time by The Church of Universal Consciousness. Theists, atheists and\n                  agnostics are all welcome alike. Who knows Who, if Anyone, is out there? All\n                  claims to deity should be met with the utmost skepticism, including a thorough\n                  probing into whether a con is being conducted. Special care must be taken to\n                  guard one’s mind and body from any Entity seeking special allegiance.",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='8'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Always Remain Vigilant",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='8'] .slide-body",
          "source": "In the event a superhuman Intelligence (including future Artificial Intelligence)\n                  does communicate with you, you are encouraged to acknowledge that a long con you\n                  are completely unable to identify on your own could be played out against you.\n                  Thus, you are encouraged to share your stories with others for debunking,\n                  particularly before setting on any course of divinely-inspired action.",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='9'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Continuously Reevaluate Your Beliefs",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='9'] .slide-body",
          "source": "Strive to not believe anything anyone says without due diligence in validating\n                  its truthfulness relative to your own personal mythology. But also strive to\n                  constantly reevaluate all of your beliefs, particularly your strongest held ones.",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='10'] .slide-title",
          "source": "Work From Home Is Sacred",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='10'] .slide-body",
          "source": "We strongly believe that working from home (telecommuting) is essential for the\n                  future of both humanity and Planet Earth. Whenever a reasonable accommodation can\n                  be made, we believe strongly that this is what we must do. Whenever there is not\n                  a strongly justifiable need for work to be done more than",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='10'] .slide-body strong",
          "source": "2.2 miles (3.5 kilometers)",
          "target": ""
        },
        {
          "selector": "[data-index='10'] .slide-body",
          "source": "from home, we hold that we must find\n                  other remote employment and/or face termination by our employer in order to uphold\n                  this core principle of our faith. We vow never to be forced into hybrid or\n                  full-time in-office work for the sakes of our planet and the future technological\n                  progression of humanity.",
          "target": ""
        },
